## 2. Anchor Layout

| LBA | Size | Head (start of device) primary → | Head fallback → |
|----|------|------|------|
| 0 | 2048 | Superblock | Superblock Backup (real second copy) |
| 1 | 2048 | Config Snapshot | unused — no second copy exists |
| 2 | 2048 | Parity Block | unused |
| 3 | 2048 | Meta/User Pointer Table | unused |
| 4 | 4096 | Function Table | unused |
| 5 | 4096 | Byte-for-byte copy of LBA4 pointer block | — |

LBA4 points to the Function Table.  
LBA5 is a copy of the LBA4 pointer block, so both point to the same Function Table LBA.

LBA0 is the only slot with a genuine second target, and it's reachable from both ends of the device (Section 12) — this is what makes the Superblock specifically hard to lose. LBA1–4's fallback fields are zero-filled and unused: there is nothing for them to point to, since Config Snapshot, the Parity Block, the Meta/User Pointer Table, and the Function Table each have exactly one on-disk copy (ADR-006).

---

## 3. Pointer Block Format

### 3.1 LBA0–3: 2048-byte pointer block

| Offset | Size | Field |
|---|---|---|
| 0–7 | 8 | magic = `"CAFSPTR\0"` (literal ASCII, byte-compared) |
| 8–15 | 8 | real_lba |
| 16–23 | 8 | real_size |
| 24–27 | 4 | checksum over bytes 0–23 |
| 28–1023 | 996 | reserved, zero |
| 1024–1031 | 8 | fallback_magic = `"CAFSPTR\0"` |
| 1032–1039 | 8 | fallback_real_lba |
| 1040–1047 | 8 | fallback_real_size |
| 1048–1051 | 4 | fallback_checksum over bytes 1024–1047 |
| 1052–2047 | 996 | reserved, zero |

### 3.2 LBA4–5: 4096-byte pointer block

Same structure, with enlarged reserved areas:

| Offset | Size | Field |
|---|---|---|
| 0–7 | 8 | magic = `"CAFSPTR\0"` (literal ASCII, byte-compared) |
| 8–15 | 8 | real_lba |
| 16–23 | 8 | real_size |
| 24–27 | 4 | checksum over bytes 0–23 |
| 28–2047 | 2020 | reserved, zero |
| 2048–2055 | 8 | fallback_magic = `"CAFSPTR\0"` |
| 2056–2063 | 8 | fallback_real_lba |
| 2064–2071 | 8 | fallback_real_size |
| 2072–2075 | 4 | fallback_checksum over bytes 2048–2071 |
| 2076–4095 | 2020 | reserved, zero |

### 3.3 Pointer Block Checksum

| ID | Algorithm |
|----|-----------|
| 1 | CRC32C — default |
| 2 | XXHASH32 |

- Primary checksum: computed over bytes 0–23.
- Fallback checksum: computed over bytes 1024–1047 for 2048-byte blocks (Section 3.1), or bytes 2048–2071 for 4096-byte blocks (Section 3.2).

