## 17c. Changes from v19 (format_version 4 → 5)

- Corrected Section 12 (End-of-Device Backup): removed the four fictional backup structures (Config Snapshot Backup, Meta/User Table Backup, Function Table Backup, Backup Parity Block) introduced in error at v17b. Only Superblock has a genuine second copy — matches ADR-006 as originally accepted, amended 2026-09-06 to spell this out explicitly.
- Split Recovery Order Track B (Section 14) into B1 (Superblock, two recovery paths) and B2 (Config Snapshot, one path) to match the corrected redundancy model; Track C now goes straight to fsck, no intermediate backup-copy step.
- Fixed pointer block magic value throughout (Section 2, 3): literal 8-byte ASCII `"CAFSPTR\0"`, not the invalid hex literal `0xCAFSPTR` used in earlier versions (ADR-010).
- Stated global little-endian byte order explicitly (Decision 9) — previously only stated for `sequence_number`.
- Added five new critical-tier structures, all pointed from the Meta/User Pointer Table: Identifier Table (7a), B-tree namespace resolution — mechanism only, byte layout still open (7b), Zone Table redefinition with per-block refcount (7c), Dedup Table — formalized with an actual byte layout for the first time (7d), Snapshot Table (7e), plus their shared Reference Counting Protocol (7f) and Snapshot Protocol (7g).
- Added two new Function Table fields: `hash_table_lba` (8a) and `recent_zero_queue_lba` (8b).
- Resolved the data block / B-tree node checksum trailer format (15a) — previously an open gap.
- Corrected Section 13.3 (In-Place Content Update) to match Section 12's fix — only Superblock gets a backup-copy write step.

